* Conventional regulated-cascode TIA (Park-Yoo style), worst-case sized
* LTspice: File > Open (All files) > this .net > Run.  Keep ptm90.lib in this folder.
* One analysis at a time: un-comment the one you want with ";" removed.
.include ptm90.lib
.temp 35

Vdd vdd 0 dc 1
Cpd in 0 450f
CL out 0 50f
Iin 0 in dc 0 ac 1
Ibn vdd vbn dc 20u
Mdn vbn vbn 0 0 nmos90 W=1u L=200n AD=0.2p AS=0.2p PD=2.4u PS=2.4u
Cbn vbn 0 2p
Mb in vbn 0 0 nmos90 W=23.9u L=200n AD=4.779p AS=4.779p PD=48.19u PS=48.19u
M1 out x in 0 nmos90 W=20.83u L=100n AD=4.166p AS=4.166p PD=42.06u PS=42.06u
R1 vdd out 635.71
M2 x in 0 0 nmos90 W=40u L=100n AD=8p AS=8p PD=80.4u PS=80.4u
R2 vdd x 811.42

.ac dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.noise V(out) Iin dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.op
;Eye diagram: open the matching _eye.net file instead (transient with a PRBS7 current source).
.meas AC zt0 FIND mag(V(out)) AT 10Meg
.meas AC zpk MAX mag(V(out))
.meas AC f3db WHEN mag(V(out))=zt0/sqrt(2) FALL=1
.backanno
.end
